    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1108">

                <pb facs="1148" n="1136" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/6–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-05T12:00:00-04:00">June 5,
                            1945—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2528. In June 4 Bonnet delivered text of message, dated June 1 but delayed in
                    transmission, from General de Gaulle to the President on the subject of the
                    situation in the Levant. Text follows in separate cable.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d1108-f1"/> Please convey the following reply to General de Gaulle
                    in the President’s name: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Through the courtesy of the French Ambassador I have received your
                            message of June 1 with regard to the situation in the Levant. I have
                            noted the orders which you have issued to the French forces there and
                            share your hope that the situation will now be susceptible of solution
                            by peaceful means.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
